  "authorization": "User explicitly requested fixing the identified deletion/close defect, committing and pushing.",
  "contract": "Normal close must retain the window while any owned book deletion or existing import/audit operation remains active. Success or failure releases only that deletion. The user can retry close after all operations finish; completion does not close automatically.",
  "implementation": {
    "query": "apps/windows/src/stores/library.ts: busy() reads the existing busy flag and owned deletion set without adding a second mutable state.",
    "consumer": "apps/windows/src/lifecycle.ts: close() checks busy() before flushing progress or destroying the window.",
    "ownership": "Existing deleteBook() owns deletion from before waiting on issued progress until its finally block; duplicate deletion requests do not acquire or release ownership."
  },
  "regressions": [
    "Real Shelf.confirmDelete with pending native deletion, repeated close requests, duplicate deletion and successful completion.",
    "Deletion waiting on issued progress, native failure, retained book and queued progress saved on a later close.",
    "Overlapping deletions and independent busy work retain protection until every owner finishes."
  ],
